# Interactive build architecture selector

Implement `tools/build/arch.py` as a minimal checklist window that lets the
user select one or more supported build targets and saves the decision to
`.cache/build/data/arch.json`.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Offer Android ARM64, iOS ARM64, Linux ARM64, Linux AMD64, macOS ARM64,
  Windows ARM64, and Windows AMD64 as the canonical initial target set.
- [ ] Investigate macOS x86-64 only as an optional compatibility target if
  current Unreal and toolchain support makes it straightforward; do not
  block macOS ARM64 on it.
- [ ] Require at least one selected target, permit selecting every supported
  target, and expose one minimal Save action.
- [ ] Write a versioned `.cache/build/data/arch.json`; manual edits are
  unsupported but must remain schema-validatable by the build runner.

## Dependencies

No explicit task dependency is required beyond the declared repository and
platform prerequisites.

## Evidence

Add implementation, deterministic validation, and supported-host evidence here
as the task advances.
